{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217263-what-are-you-running-playing-right-now","id":1217263,"title":"What are you running/playing right now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-09T21:27:29-07:00","id":1217263,"title":"What are you running/playing right now?","content":"Since 3E Dragon-Bloods are only just now going to come out and the other major splats are nowhere in sight, I was just curious to know what exactly are people actually playing in their Series? <br /> <br /> Do you even have your Solars encounter any other Exalt type out there or are you veering away from such things until/if 3E rules for these characters are released? <br /> <br /> I'm just curious to know how Storytellers handle any of it. <br /> <br /> Like what do your characters <i>do</i> this whole time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T23:03:05-07:00","id":1217279,"title":"","content":"My campaign started out as an attempt to homage shounen anime, and thus opened with a PvP martial arts tournament. A Wyld Hunt crashed the tournament before the final round, and I dodged having to work out mechanics for the Sidereal-Martial-Arts-wielding BronzeSid leading the Hunt by having her and the SMA-wielding GoldSid who hosted the tournament cancel each other out. The rest of the Hunt was run with Core Quick Character stats.<br /> <br /> From there, the party sailed to Champoor, got tied up in a bunch of divine / criminal intrigue, and is currently in the process of fighting <i>multiple</i> gods. I'm using Fakharu's statblock from Core for Tenepeshu herself, and I also worked in a few other Core statblocks (Fogsharks, Greenmaws, a grab bag of mortals) during their time in the city, but I've had to cobble together stats for some of the gods myself.<br /> <br /> After Champoor... well, some of my players read these forums, so I can't get too detailed, but I <i>am</i> planning to use some more non-Solar, non-DB Exalts. Martial Arts and Evocations are useful for any types, you can sorta fake Abyssals with Solar Charms... right now I think using Lunar NPCs would be the biggest challenge, but thankfully they're next in line.<br /> <br /> Oh, I will say that I thiiiiiink the Sidereal Excellency in Core is broken. They're weak on defense since they can never add more than (Essence) to a static value, but the Target Number reduction is <i>very</i> efficient. Bending fate to work in their favor is core enough to their concept I don't think I can get rid of it entirely, but I I'm going to try capping it at TN 5, rather than 4, next time a Sidereal rolls against my players. We'll see if that's enough or if it needs further tweaking. (Maybe a cost adjustment.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T23:28:38-07:00","id":1217281,"title":"","content":"I am currently running a game set in River Province that was a Mortal Chronicle and is transitioning into a Solar one. The player characters are dealing with multiple threats: two different demon cults, some hungry Fair Folk, and the main antagonist is the Deathlord Mask of Winters. Its very much a Classic style Exalted game using EX3 rules and setting updates, that very much character-driven and focused on the township the player-characters call home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T00:26:48-07:00","id":1217287,"title":"","content":"My players are all new to Exalted, and we've only had our first session. We'll do one a month i think. We play in the West, and will do a lot of island hopping. <br /> <br /> So far, they are on tutorial island, learning mechanics. They were all at a festival when it was attacked by bandits looking for a relic, so now they're caught up in plot to secure a key to a long lost mausoleum, which has sunk into a swamp. The Mausoleum has a really powerful &quot;call&quot; to the Underworld so ghosts and nightmare beasts are flocking there, causing a shadowlands taint. <br /> <br /> There are 3 challenges ahead of them, related to Fire, Wind, and Wood (Mausoleum is Earth). After &quot;fixing&quot; all 4 challenges, the elemental restraints of an ancient Leviathan will be broken by a Deathlord who used the essence of them solving the elemental challenges as a geomantic lockbreaker. The freed leviathan will cause a massive rampage. <br /> <br /> Thats the main story for Arc 1. Arc 2 will deal with the fallout of that and the Realm using it as a casus belli to &quot;pacify&quot; the West<br /> <br /> Edit: antagonists. So far, bandits and zombies. An Abyssal made a big enterance at the last minute of play and is about to fight the Solars. He has a Liminal flunkie and a Golem undead construct. Maybe a 2nd abyssal. Lotta ghosts coming up, then depending on what they do, elementals, brass soldiers, Realm Navy, a god or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-10-2018, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T01:07:43-07:00","id":1217291,"title":"","content":"TBH, I did find the lack of books annoying, which was one of the reasons I stopped running it.<br /> <br /> When I did run the game, the PCs started with a plot where their friend had been kidnapped by a coven of sorcerers, the Ascended. Mostly mortal sorcerers (with first circle demon lackeys), but one Dragonblood and one Lunar (though they never found out about the Lunar). So sorcery helped replace charms to some extent.<br /> <br /> Then they essentially had a choice, with clues to three different groups of enemies. The one already mentioned (but they'd mostly smashed them), the Sons of Shadow (an Ebon-Dragon cult, so I could use demons like Mara and Alveua, or just make my own), or the Crimson Masters, a fanatical Cult of the Illuminated-schismatic sect leading a horde of barbarian horsemen, the Crimson Horde.<br /> <br /> They ended up going after the Crimson Masters, so my antagonists were mostly Solars leading battle groups of Tiger Warriors.<br /> <br /> I'd say the game went well, but honestly, other than the Solar NPCs themselves, I found it a bit frustrating how little there was to oppose players (I should say this game was Essence 4, as it was a continuation of our 2nd ed game; it might have been easier for me if they'd been Essence 1. I haven't played an 0xp of Exalted for like 7 years though).<br /> <br /> So now I'm running Star Wars instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> But my friend has just restarted my old game, and he's setting us up to fight the Realm (which I always had in the background for when the book came out), which should be good. For now (as the book hadn't come out when he started) we're hunting moonsilver tuplas. I guess he's just made up the rules himself. We also fought some elementals and a Hydra (well, the Dawn fought the Hydra) which bled hungry ghosts. That was cool.<br /> <br /> So, basically, so far, sorcerers, custom monsters/spirits, and Solars.<br /> <br /> You could also do a game with Abyssals as the main antagonists, and just use the rules for Solars. But my 2nd ed game had Walker in Darkness as the Big Bad, so I didn't want to use Abyssals again.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also play another game, in which I play a monk (Alazar) from the Black Monastery of Leng, who came to the party to learn kung-fu so he could go back and defeat the Nephwrack known as He Who Shall Not Be Described, who took over his monastery and sent the other monks insane.<br /> The STs run with it, so we've mostly been fighting/investigating ghosts, spectres, mortwrights, etc, and we're hunting a Nephwrack. We also fought some giant acid-spitting worm-monsters on our way to the monastery,<br /> <br /> That group is not very combat-optimised (though they're not terrible) so we don't need really powerful foes. But we're still Essence 4 Celestials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:35:28-07:00","id":1217371,"title":"","content":"I have a Hundred Kingdoms semi-sandbox campaign on hiatus. It started in the playtests and sort of got bogged down without a proper, full version of the core book (we didn't have access to leaks and used only a few documents with mechanical excerpts). Gotta restart that one when I'll have a bit more free time...<br /> <br /> Recently, though, I'm running a one-player campaign for my wife. She plays a mortal customs officer slash investigator working for the Peleps satrap in Wu-Jian. In due time she is supposed to exalt as an Eclipse, but right now we're having a lot of fun with not a single Exalt appearing for six sessions straight since we started (just one mortal sorcerer and his summoned blood ape).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3751-ferozstein","name":"Ferozstein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3751_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:53:21-07:00","id":1217377,"title":"","content":"My group consists of 3 Solars, 1 Lunar and 1 Alchemical PC. So far they've interacted with mortals, ghosts, gods, Dragon-Blooded, and Alchemicals. They've decided not to interact with Lunars, I think my Lunar player is (probably rightly) scared of her elders. <br /> <br /> To be more specific, they've followed the scavenger lord Sin Welldon (OC) in search of the Manses of Kal Bax (canon), treated with the salt gods (canon) and Golden Eyed Jorst's majordomo (OC), they've worked under false aliases for Miss Tachibana Yito (Earth Aspected OC) of Calin (canon), commissioned Nellens Baiden and his ship (canon), and encountered the Patropolis of Ot (canon) and the intrepid explorers of First Contact, Eternally Vigilant Bell, Voice of Authority, Blinding Light of Progress, and the Starmetal Caste I can't remember right now (semi-canon) as well as their Assembly leader, Colossus-Class Soulsteel Caste Everything That Power Permits (OC).<br /> <br /> I happen to have run a few 2e games, and thus own 2e books, so I just translate content over to 3e mechanics when I need something. Also, Sandcat6's Alchemical homebrew has been very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:04:09-07:00","id":1217382,"title":"","content":"My players have been Solars ever since the corebook came out in one long-runnning campaign. They have now rolled DBs who are going to continue in the same setting they have already been Solars in (so their Solars are still around somewhere). We've started doing preludes where they play some school year scenes and such while we're resolving the last Solar stories. The plan is to continue playing DBs now until Lunars come out, and then have them reroll Lunars, all in the same setting. The trick I've needed to face as ST is to take notes of global changes since we've gone beyond the usual campaign starting dates by several years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:49:33-07:00","id":1217417,"title":"","content":"My game is 3 Solars who've mostly been wandering the West pursuing whatever minor issues come up in front of us.<ul><li>We've encountered pirates, which culminated in a mage duel and us taking 2 of their ships with crew and converting them from piracy.</li> <li>We've found a First Age manse dedicated to a member of our First Age circle and collected a First Age Dragonkin advisor sworn to serve us who mostly just tries to convince us to rule the world (something we're not interested in).</li> <li>We met up with a colony of Lunars who are trying to make a paradise society but are warring with the Lintha, and we've been helping out the Lunars a lot.</li> <li>We invaded a Lintha prisoner island to free prisoners and ended up in a dream trap (Tomb of Dreams scenario, modified to include the Lintha prisoners), when we emerged it was 3 months later and our ships and crew had long since left. Had to summon Tidemares to wander the west in search of comrades.</li> <li>We've captured a traitor from a player's past and returned them to their homeland for justice, found the island under the rule of sorcerously bound demons and defeated a second circle demon (with some very broken mechanical adaptations from 2e I might add, thank you Spirit-Caging Mandala for the rescue). Found out the demon was bound by our old First Age circle-mate who is alive and taunting us for some reason.</li> </ul>We're kind of in the middle of a lot of plot threads and currently undecided which way to go. But I believe my GM expects this to be a world spanning arc where we go all over towards some epic conclusion. Meaning this will likely be a 2+ year game (and we've been at it for a year already).<br /> <br /> My GM adapts Lunars based on a combination of 2e examples and core book antagonists. I tend to help him where I can with building foes because I have a better eye and patience for that kind of detail. We've only fought 1 DB and that was the Earth Immaculate straight from the back of the core book. No other types yet, but I expect my GM to just fudge stuff based on 2e as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 05-10-2018, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T09:32:40-07:00","id":1217424,"title":"","content":"We're about to finish a Solar campaign in the North. The characters haven't fought any other exalted cause we want to wait for their books to come out in the distant future. Nonetheless, there has been a lot of supernatural antagonists. We don't care about setting taxonomy, meaning that we don't need to define if a certain entity is an elemental, spirit or whatever to determine if it would or would not have enough power to face the main Solar characters. So overall we improvise stats and custom powers to make things fun for us, and don't aim to make them canon or compatible with everyone else's games or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T09:42:41-07:00","id":1217427,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing in a homebrew PBTA hack of Exalted 3E with full splat support. I'm also running/playtesting a more streamlined hack of EX3 which works on the same mechanical principles, just faster. The latter only has splat support for what the main line does. Prior to the DB book coming out we did what we did for years and just made stuff up/used the existing inspirations from previous editions (mostly 1E) to slot into the mechanical housing of QC's as a base. All I'm really getting out of the actual EX3 books are ideas and fluff, which justifies a purchase. I'm certainly not paying the writers for their mechanics.<br /> <br /> That being said, my PBTA group is running 2 Infernals, a Solar, a Sid, and a DB. We mostly bumble around and get into trouble and riff from there. Like an old-school adventuring game. My streamlined group is all Solars, one from each caste and the goal of that game is to overthrow a satrapy in the west to create an independent state able to negotiate with the realm on equal terms. Think of it like a polynesian revolution type thing. It's fun and essentially a byway for myself and my players to learn about ocean-bound cultures.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T05:49:48-07:00","id":1217639,"title":"","content":"I'm running the same game I started 10 years ago and during that time I remember that there's been <b>dozens</b> of events that would've played out differently if a particular book had come out earlier, several incidents where the lore changed pretty significantly when we'd already interacted with a previous version with very few hard retcons.<br /> <br /> I'm the only one who really remembers most of it without the assistance of logs to the point I once brought back a Sidereal as an antagonist because the PCs had forgotten about him in the Labyrinth over three years ago and the fact none of them could remember him freaked out some of the players.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I\u2019m not going to wait for books. Worst case scenario is that I get things wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T06:11:04-07:00","id":1217642,"title":"","content":"Right now, it's a starter game with a couple total newcomers, one newcomer to Exalted and my wife that knows the basics of the setting. Fairly simple and classic &quot;save the world&quot; setup with all Solars, with the team now inserting themselves inside Thorns to start up a revolution.<br /> <br /> They're taking well to the game and started a few cool things (blowing up a Daybreak's lab and his warstrider-sized flesh golem in a massive fight). There's a couple Lunars and Sids running around, and I even popped a couple Exigents in there for the hell of it. Vance's been open enough about the general system behind the splats that I play pretend well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T09:40:20-07:00","id":1217694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217263-what-are-you-running-playing-right-now?p=1217639#post1217639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm the only one who really remembers most of it without the assistance of logs to the point I once brought back a Sidereal as an antagonist because the PCs had forgotten about him in the Labyrinth over three years ago and the fact none of them could remember him freaked out some of the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, that's brilliant! Tempts me to try something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T11:27:18-07:00","id":1217729,"title":"","content":"Running the same campaign I've been running for the last two years give or take. Still not touching 3rd Edition but many things from it has trickled down into my homebrew and my group is prospering the Zenith Prophet characters is about to start a religious war in the underworld where his cult is most strongly entrenched, the Dusk caste madscientists/necromancer is cackling about soon building his warstrider army but usually gets distracted by the next plothook (Having a defining intimacy of Adventure! is really helpful), the Sidereal martial artist is a running joke as his multiple characters appear and disappear, the Wood Dragon sorcerer-priest has become the sworn champion of Siaka and that just can't go well, our Full Blood Lunar merchant-general mostly chills being reasonably invincible. They have entered an Illiad inspired area on their long travels away from their homeland, which means a lot of fun things to do and a few old enemies are going to pop up eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T14:36:22-07:00","id":1217777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217263-what-are-you-running-playing-right-now?p=1217639#post1217639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, I\u2019m not going to wait for books. Worst case scenario is that I get things wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And sometimes great stories may come from playing with making wrong right - or a whole new sort of right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Last game i played, due to a combination of being a late arrival and some frequency limitations, intead of a sixth Solar i joined as the Twilight sorcererss' Blood Ape familiar and the circle was involved with the travails of an archipelago/empire going through a decades long civil war and how a number of individual island powers seemed to be out of their way to make things worse for everybody through deals with the supernatural in a variety of ways. We dealt with gods, playful or nasty, a curiously nice neomah just wanting to live in peaceful leisure in Creation as a nun maintaining a house for war orphans (she still made extra children out of habit, but most people concluded were just more foundlings), a guerilla group ancestor cult selling people as slaves to the fae in exchange for magical objects and weaponry, a sorcerer seeking out a group of lost manses, the prisons/resting places of the tenebrous demon princes, the fruits of a First Age sorcerer - particular brand of exalted unclear - experiments with both duplicating the souls of Erembour and devising whole new unimagined beings from division and recombination of the original into variant clones, for a (supposed) whole total of 49 pseudo-second circle demons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-11-2018, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T14:39:26-07:00","id":1217778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217263-what-are-you-running-playing-right-now?p=1217694#post1217694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, that's brilliant! Tempts me to try something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh, just had a similar experience a couple hours ago. The players don't know about Sids, but one of them did get a &quot;omnious prediction of doom from a forgettable seer&quot; a couples months back. The Sid just popped up right at their front door, and nobody even remembered the artwork enough to make the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T06:09:22-07:00","id":1217945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217263-what-are-you-running-playing-right-now?p=1217777#post1217777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sometimes great stories may come from playing with making wrong right - or a whole new sort of right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also very much in favour of &quot;cheating&quot; for a good cause.<br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of otherwise good Storytellers continue to straight jacket themselves by insisting on designing NPCs like PCs then being frustrated by the result because they're trying to achieve different objectives to the charmset.<br /> <br /> Safety Among Enemies is the most recent charm that's highlighted this design quirk for me, it has a number of limitations that encourages you to use it very ruthlessly and direct decisive attacks towards crashed enemies, that kind of behaviour from an NPC could leave you with one dead PC and another to blame for it. ...we've got a canonical story of a circle imploding over this and Demetheus' characterisation getting badly derailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T05:46:29-07:00","id":1218180,"title":"","content":"My 2nd 3E Game kicked off this weekend, we didn't get much done in the first session, except getting all characters from Non-Trivial Mortal to Solar, which is of course pretty good in setting the tone. So kind of a drawn-out prelude, that set a pretty fun tone between cthulhuid horror and a little bit of slapstick, and an overarching theme of focus on the Little Gods of Creation.<br /> Unsurprisingly, this game is set in Great Forks, at least so far, going Vanilla for once in our lives. The last game we ran was in the Dreaming Sea, which is an obvious starting point for anyone's first 3E game.<br /> <br /> We actually accidentally made a Perfect Circle, where everyone, without talking to each other, wanted to play a different caste, which was funny in itself. We, then, of course coordinated to make the characters vaguely compatible with each other, because we're nice people.<br /> <br /> The circle consists, as far as I can judge by now, of:<br /> <br /> - The Dawn, a Marukani warrior-prince with the giant merit, a god-blooded horse, and great skill with both bow and blade, who had his clan eaten by the walking dead, who is kind of a goody-two-shoes, until he goes Conan all over everybody's asses. Enjoys a good pillaging, but is really a nice guy in the end. (Melee Supernal)<br /> <br /> - The Zenith, who was sold as a child-slave to a Fae that was more &quot;The Ritual&quot; than it was anything vaguely cute, and raised by them as a living weapon to be set lose on the threshold, where she was bound by powerful geases to drive spurned lovers to suicide, and who has only broken free of her bond through Exaltation. She was initiated into Sorcery by the Raksha who kept her, and wields reality-warping powers through her initiation, which she despises, because she hates the Wyld. Performance supernal, and possibly unstable.<br /> <br /> - The Twilight, a ghost-talker from a forgotten swamp tribe in the northeast, guided by a wisp and the spirits of her deceased family, in a never-ending crusade against the Neverborn, She wields the knowledge of her ancestors as a weapon, and has sworn to throw the Neverborn and her Deathlord servants into the Void once and for all. Occult supernal, and probably the sane one of the group.<br /> <br /> - The Night, who insists he is a prince, or emperor, of some sort and had his Dominion stolen along with his memory, carrying around a magical book that contains his recovered memories. Has a potentially evil servant that is summoned by his book, and seems like kind of a swell guy. Is Larceny supernal, and strongly suspected of being really evil, if he ever regained his memory.<br /> <br /> - The Eclipse, a fertility godesses priestess and divine matchmaker, who has brokered marriages for her entire life, most of which have ended in death of one of the spouses, if not separation of some sort - a shortcoming of Creation she intensely wishes to rectify, either by fixing relationships, or removing them from the equation in entirety. She is a delight, Socialize supernal, and possibly on the verge of becoming a super villain in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T06:07:58-07:00","id":1218185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217263-what-are-you-running-playing-right-now?p=1217945#post1217945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also very much in favour of &quot;cheating&quot; for a good cause.<br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of otherwise good Storytellers continue to straight jacket themselves by insisting on designing NPCs like PCs then being frustrated by the result because they're trying to achieve different objectives to the charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, constant sticking to going by RAW has a far from insignificant risk of surprise messes hitting the PCs - and more importantly, any dreams of the ST of plot direction - like a triphammer to the face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217263-what-are-you-running-playing-right-now?p=1217945#post1217945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safety Among Enemies is the most recent charm that's highlighted this design quirk for me, it has a number of limitations that encourages you to use it very ruthlessly and direct decisive attacks towards crashed enemies, that kind of behaviour from an NPC could leave you with one dead PC and another to blame for it. ...we've got a canonical story of a circle imploding over this and Demetheus' characterisation getting badly derailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say derail per se, more like leading him in a major personal crisis of sorts - what can also be good roleplaying fodder, the Twelve Labors spring out of a similar motive, so to speak - but i can see what you mean about the weird turns Demetheus as a drunken wreck out of guilt subplot took.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-13-2018, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T06:55:03-07:00","id":1218195,"title":"","content":"I am running a game that started in the South, where the players decided to elevate a town and commercially take over a big city, giving themselves the duty of giving people better lives. They do that via a ton of intrigue, undermining the opposition, making structural upgrades and the occasional bellic display. Currently they moved East, their merc company got hired to participate in a small civil war on an old loyal satrapy. Their zenith is quivering with antiipation to get his troops to smash some legionnaires. Their dawn too, but he is passing time harassing enemy scouts, taming moas to form a cavalry and hitting on the twilight.<br /> Here there's been a couple sidereals and several DBs, but people avoided confrontation so far, a mix of fear, uncertainty, ambitions...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am playing in a game that just started... and hasn't gone anywhere because happenstance kept the last 3 games from lasting more than a couple hours &gt;.&gt; But we had time to establish and get the hang of our characters' basic personality traits. My Dawn is a vain, dickish tya merc that will see her bellicose joie de vivre create a following (and I have no idea how that will affect her), we have a surly foreign assassin trying to establish a foothold in wujian (his order is the assassins' to the immaculate order's templars) and AnnoyingBrat!Daedalus, whose player is having fun messing with the shift of innocence. The next couple games will probably revolve around the assassin's goals, for he's hiring local help and I'm it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 05-13-2018, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:06:30-07:00","id":1220006,"title":"","content":"We've parked Exalted for a bit, so we can finish up other hanging campaigns and wait for Lunars to at least get previewy. <br /> <br /> In the meanwhile, the cinematic combat style in E3 (especially Momentum converted, plug plug) has me rethinking a lot of our gameplay tropes in many genres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T16:07:52-07:00","id":1220126,"title":"","content":"currently in the planning process of a 3e solar game, first go at 3rd ed and admittedly as my first go at being the storyteller, wish me luck, played quite a bit of 2nd ed though, starting in the hundred kingdoms, not sure where I'm going to take the game after that though, going to talk to the players during character gen about which bits of the setting they want to explore, and then wrangle more long term plot in that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}